Z||000009||kslish||06-26-2001||03:51 PM||||Hmmm...surprise surprise.  Figures, and I was hoping FOCOA was getting their act together.  As I've been going to some of the Fiero shows this year I've been hearing a lot of bitterness toward FOCOA and how either a new properly run national club needs to be formed or one of the large local clubs needs to go national.  A national car club should be around for the betterment of the hobby, and the current one seems to be dividing it and making enemies.  <P>Without a national club with many different people involved, it can't stay around long term.  What would happen to the club if something unfortunate would happen to Phil or Gloria or one of them becomes sick?  Who would pick up the slack?<P>On a side note I heard a rumor this weekend that Phil may dissolve the Board of Directors that was formed a few years back because they haven't accomplished much.  I wonder if that is the case....my theory is that the Board doesn't have enough freedom to get the job done.<P>I've seen the Fiero Owners of America, the Worldwide Fiero Club, and some others die a slow death and FOCOA seems to be heading the same direction.  It shouldn't be this way.  It's not as if the member base isn't there, I see the national Covair club and others thriving with a much smaller membership base.<P>All this may make Williamsburg and interesting show...<P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cheever2||06-26-2001||04:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>surprise surprise.  Figures, and I was hoping FOCOA was getting their act together. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I agree with both of you.  I was waiting to see what the change is like before joining, but now I think the new boss will be the same as the old boss. <P>If you get any bright ideas about something <I>different</I> you want to try, I'll support you.<P>"We don't get fooled again" - <I>The Who</I><P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||fieroshop||06-26-2001||04:19 PM||||I guess that I will have to put my 2 cents on this subject.<BR>You heard wrong and a new site is being done for the Club not the business.<BR>FOCOA is two parts and one being the club and the other the business. Gloria took it upon herself to get this site up as there was nothing out there at all. In Williamsburg there will be a decision at the governing board meeting to decide exactly what will be done and when. Those are the facts as I know them, I am the Western Regional Director for FOCOA. I repeat The FOCOA SHOP AND THE FOCOA CLUB SITES WILL BE DIFFERENT.<P>I prefer not to discuss this on the Forum but anyone wishing more information may call me toll free at 866-534-8486 <P>------------------<BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
